<p>The May agents were accessing different files (mostly local UK government data), but these files are very similar in character to those pursued by the wiki agents. Moreover, they use the same retrieval methods. 1,397 packages mention <a href="http://r.jina.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">r.jina.ai</a>, which was used heavily by the agents on the wiki. We also see that many packages mention <a href="http://example.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">example.com</a>, which wiki agents used to test their posting ability.</p>
<p>Our understanding from talking to people in the RubyGems community is that <b>OpenAI never informed them </b>that they were responsible for this attack.</p>
